{"c":[{"id":"ce92a517b2f97b48","sum":"B24-W3: <select> hand-off; memory.ndjson=helper golden; unrestorable clipboard blocks paste; page snapshot mirrors Chrome AX; bridge->host via XPC only; accept.ts: --sign-identity, temp launchd host; memory .md grants no authority; U+2028 escapes for oxc; push v2/* to sam.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f48370a3611e6add","sum":"B24, I2-I3, W3: person-details fill = 4 Jev calls; Groq 429s; TextEdit opens files from its Containers tmp; <select> is a hand-off; memory.ndjson = helper golden; unrestorable clipboard blocks paste; page snapshot mirrors Chrome AX; Helium NMH dir; page.sock proofs bind pid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8d81c7b9a87754a7","sum":"B24, I3: person-details fill = 4 Jev calls (PER_FILL); Groq 429s, space writer calls 30 s; TextEdit opens files only from its Containers tmp; native <select> is a value-less hand-off; host memory.ndjson = helper golden, find lines by id.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d32f644355f794d8","sum":"B24: a person-details fill asks twice (whose, then values): 4 Jev calls, PER_FILL in counting tests; Groq qwen3.8 429s within ~20 plans, space writer calls 30 s; sandboxed TextEdit opens files only from its Containers tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-05aef102d22989aa","text":"B24: fill asks in two stages when a field takes a person's details (whose first, then values), so a fill is 4 Jev calls, not 2; tests that count calls use PER_FILL. Groq's qwen3.8 hits 429 token limits within ~20 plans; space writer calls 30 s.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T192504Z-2947a2d88b908a7e","text":"B24: TextEdit is sandboxed: a file named on its command line opens only from inside ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp (realfill-capture.ts makes its own folder there and deletes it).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e9b74ce9f7778aba","sum":"B24, I3: Chrome AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton with only the chosen option, so fill hands selects off with no value; host Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper golden byte for byte; tests find lines by id, never index.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-d09a0e8b1bd722e1","text":"B24: Chrome's AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton whose only child is the selected option; the option list is not readable without opening it, so fill names selects as hand-offs with no value (capture-2 probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195224Z-8ef6ab64ee3f2dea","text":"I3: apps/caret Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper's golden byte for byte as of H1 (host-memory-5 request added, A16's wrote line is host-memory-9, no -8); tests find lines by id, never by index.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3093b549fb68152a","sum":"I2-I3, W3: paste refused for unrestorable clipboard types; page-link snapshot mirrors Chrome AX; Helium reads NMH manifests from its --user-data-dir; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"787299ed8ad30f01","sum":"I2-I3: paste route refused when the prior clipboard holds a type outside restorableTypes (AX write, else clipboardUnrestorable); page-link toWindowSnapshot must mirror Chrome AX (AXTimeField, radios under an AXGroup per name, select options as AXMenuItem).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T195224Z-99ff86984f364892","text":"I3: host refuses the paste route when the prior clipboard holds a type outside ReconcilingClipboard.restorableTypes (file URL, private types): AX write instead, else fail clipboardUnrestorable. A17's VM probe lost a file-url item 5/5 while restore said restored.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195842Z-c30fb40a821e024f","text":"I2: page-link.ts toWindowSnapshot must match Chrome AX for fill/controls.ts: time is AXTimeField, radios sit under an AXGroup per name attribute, select options are AXMenuItem children. PageControl has no fieldset legend, so page radio groups have no label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"13ae7e710e2343cf","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads NMH manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; both page.sock proofs (bridgeProof too) bind the helper pid, or a socket swap keeps the host's session.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-5a96910dba2d6b69","text":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads Native Messaging manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts (accept.ts --browser passes 42/42); its Web Store page offers Add to Helium.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-74ab7d13fad22cf2","text":"W3: page.sock proofs both bind the helper pid (bridgeProof too), or a same-user process that swaps the socket path can pass the host's hello to the real helper and keep that session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"07a41b3f18dd2c1e","sum":"W3/memory: bridge->host via XPC only; accept.ts needs --sign-identity, runs a temp launchd host; headless CfT focus sticks to CDP windows; XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; memory .md grants no authority (sqlite rules);   escapes for oxc; push v2/* to sam.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eddb660e4954b5f4","sum":"W3, memory: bridge reaches the host over XPC only; accept.ts needs --sign-identity and runs a temp launchd host; headless CfT focus sticks to CDP windows; XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; memory markdown goes to the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94d9cdb89929ed3f","sum":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the host over XPC, never page.sock; accept.ts needs --sign-identity (and --other-identity) and boots out its temp launchd host; headless CfT focuses a CDP-created window and activateTarget won't move it back.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-903b513efe20fc90","text":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the Caret host over XPC (CaretBridgeXPC), never page.sock; no <sock>.key exists. accept.ts needs --sign-identity <team SHA-1> (and --other-identity for refusal checks) and runs caret-bridge-testhost as a temporary launchd job it boots out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-98052ff285eab267","text":"W3: headless Chrome for Testing gives focus to a window CDP Target.createTarget opens and Target.activateTarget does not move it back; chrome.windows focused is reported in headless. Page window focus = active tab of the focused, last-focused window.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3, memory: a client's setCodeSigningRequirement guards replies, not its first send, so XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; personal memory is markdown in <dir>/Memory, the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4ac352ed8f3af9fe","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (state stays in memory.sqlite; fileDigest catches offline edits); write \\u2028 escapes for oxc; push v2/* to remote sam, never origin; B25: Ask on INTENT_ROUTE gpt-oss-120b, plans on WRITER_ROUTE qwen3.8 (Groq daily cap).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, clean runs stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill file puts it back on Tab; fileDigest catches offline edits). vite's oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal: write the escape.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2ebd6c0099fdfde","sum":"Push v2/* to remote sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret); origin is the team hackathon repo. B25: Ask intents use INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plans WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day runs out in dev; gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T210855Z-22a0908ac8155d26","text":"Push v2/* branches to the remote named sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret), where their PRs live. origin is the team hackathon repo (theodorexli/hackathon-2026-09-19); a bare 'git push origin' publishes there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-2bd567d78f578d5c","text":"B25: Ask intents go to INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs to WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day ran out during dev runs, and gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400 'does not match the expected schema'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a3b90a5982d0edfb","sum":"U1: panels +24pt for shadow (not desk); contrast gated from pixels; mkdir ModelRuntime/Vendor first. T2 range edits AX-only. build-app.sh holds build.lock (CARET_NO_LOCK under lockf); Caret.app starts own services unless a socket is named; acting debug cmds need --test-hooks.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"41a7747c68ff4b5e","sum":"U1: panel windows +24 pt for shadow except the desk; ContrastRenderTests gate contrast from pixels; off-screen NSHostingView has no a11y tree; mkdir ModelRuntime/Vendor before llama.xcframework. Never-typed kinds: memory/sensitive.ts only. T2 range edits are AX-only, never paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b12c5adbb4da292e","sum":"U1: panel frames are the content's; windows +24 pt for shadow except the desk (margin 0). ContrastRenderTests gate 4.5 text / 3 marks from pixels. Off-screen NSHostingView has no a11y tree: test via SlipSpeech. Setup: mkdir ModelRuntime/Vendor before copying llama.xcframework.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"caa08afcda9d84a4","sum":"U1: HostedPanel frames are the content's; windows are 24 pt larger for the drawn shadow, except interactive panels (desk: margin 0, system shadow). ContrastRenderTests measure token contrast from rendered pixels; a slip under 4.5 text / 3 marks fails there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T205314Z-27bd8497da5b0b8f","text":"U1 v3: HostedPanel frames (size, pin, debugInfo) are the content's; the window is 24 pt larger for the drawn shadow, except interactive panels (the desk), which keep margin 0 and the system shadow so the margin never eats clicks.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T205315Z-15530fcef19ed7a7","text":"U1: token contrast is measured from rendered pixels by ContrastRenderTests (Tokens.hidden blanks one token; changed pixels are its glyphs, the hidden render is their ground); a token change that drops a slip under 4.5 text / 3 marks fails there.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e56ade2067e19a9","sum":"Worktree setup: mkdir packages/keytype/Packages/ModelRuntime/Vendor before copying llama.xcframework, or Vendor becomes the framework. Off-screen NSHostingView has no a11y tree; test slip labels via SlipSpeech, count elements only on screen (VM).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T205315Z-c430e28338d1fa45","text":"Worktree setup: copying llama.xcframework into packages/keytype/Packages/ModelRuntime/Vendor/ when Vendor does not exist makes Vendor the framework (SwiftPM: 'does not contain a binary artifact'); mkdir Vendor first.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T205315Z-d04a530977d6b116","text":"U1: SwiftUI builds no accessibility tree for an NSHostingView that is not on screen (accessibilityChildren is empty even after cacheDisplay); test slip labels through SlipSpeech, count elements only on screen (VM).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d3c90c2874f43484","sum":"B25: spaced eval calls need a fresh AbortSignal; realfill strips U+2731 from labels. Never-typed kinds: extend memory/sensitive.ts only. T2: writing marks bind to their checked sentence (an edit there drops one); range edits are AX-only (select, revalidate, verify), never paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b1d476e32a92cb95","sum":"B25: eval writers that space calls need a fresh AbortSignal after the wait (a 15 s gap aborted every intent). The job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it (B24 scoreboards missed those four fields).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-3925313f151b5275","text":"B25: eval writers that space calls must give the request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait; a 15 s gap aborted every intent in planner-eval's first GUI run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-9174d67891bff255","text":"B25: the job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it, and B24's scoreboards counted those four fields as not found.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a514cda7aa8cec1f","sum":"Never-typed kinds live in memory/sensitive.ts (M1); extend it, no second list. T2: writing fixes are OfferKind.writing; a mark binds to its checked sentence, any edit there drops it; range edits are AX-only (select, revalidate, AXSelectedText, verify), never paste.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-bc8230171f42cb4e","text":"B25: never-typed kinds (fill, planner, Ask) are memory/sensitive.ts, M1's classifier copied unchanged from v2/memory; extend that file, never a second list.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T212904Z-afa8d900ec44c553","text":"T2: writing fixes are OfferKind.writing; a mark is bound to its checked sentence (WritingMarks), so any edit in that sentence (or its '. ' before) drops it; range edits are AX-only (select, revalidate, AXSelectedText, caret back, verify), never paste.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfcfde6b45075d98","sum":"Spelling uses US/GB/CA witnesses; build-app.sh holds build.lock (CARET_NO_LOCK=1 under lockf); SIP off here; Caret.app starts own services unless a socket is named, tests use --home; acting debug commands need --test-hooks; captcha HSTS; SO_NOSIGPIPE; Groq TPD 429s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b3ea4773732e5218","sum":"T2: NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA witnesses (en_AU accepts 'seperate'); NSSpellChecker may autocorrect to guess 2. H4: build-app.sh holds build.lock (CARET_NO_LOCK=1 under lockf); SIP is off here; Caret.app starts its own services unless a socket is named; tests pass --home.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cc86c50101fc2328","sum":"T2: en_AU accepts 'seperate'/'truely', so NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA witnesses; NSSpellChecker may autocorrect to its 2nd guess (adress->dress). H4: build-app.sh holds build.lock all run; callers under heavy.sh/lockf set CARET_NO_LOCK=1; release/acceptance need IDENTITY.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T212904Z-f841172a94ee81e8","text":"T2: macOS 26.6's en_AU spell dictionary accepts 'seperate' and 'truely'; NativeChecker uses US/GB/CA as regional witnesses and en-AU only when the user lists it. In context NSSpellChecker can autocorrect to its 2nd guess ('adress' -> dress while guess 1 is address).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220029Z-2e8d5e2431d5ac81","text":"H4: build-app.sh takes build.lock for the whole run (compile, copy, sign); a caller already under heavy.sh or lockf sets CARET_NO_LOCK=1 or it deadlocks. release and acceptance need IDENTITY (team cert SHA-1); debug is ad hoc.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0b2cc0daa10616a1","sum":"H4: SIP is off on Sam's Mac, so hardened runtime/library validation aren't enforced; measure entitlements on a SIP-on Mac. A built Caret.app starts its own helper and reader unless --helper-socket or CARET_SCREEN_SOCKET names one; test runs pass --home DIR.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T220029Z-8a608f67782b76c4","text":"H4: SIP is disabled on Sam's Mac (csrutil status), so the hardened runtime and library validation are not enforced there; node.entitlements (allow-jit only) and any entitlement question must be measured on a SIP-on Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220029Z-91a1d68b9a61d85a","text":"H4: a built Caret.app starts its own helper and reader unless --helper-socket or CARET_SCREEN_SOCKET names one; test runs of a bundle pass --home DIR (sockets, data, host.sock and settings move there) and never run with neither.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"030d4823d12628cf","sum":"Debug socket key/control/click/settings set need --test-hooks. Captcha hosts are HSTS: test frames via compose.ts unit tests. Bridge Swift tests share a process: test sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE. Groq one-token probes pass with TPD spent; only real-size requests show 429.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"90700581377d9b92","sum":"CodeRabbit #9: the debug socket refuses key, control, click and settings set without --test-hooks; key-driving scripts pass it. W4: captcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so a test browser can't map them to local http; test captcha frames via extension compose.ts unit tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T220029Z-fe7551bbc4c0644b","text":"CodeRabbit #9: the host debug socket refuses key, control, click and settings set without --test-hooks (HostRuntime.testHookRefusal); acceptance scripts that drive keys start the host with --test-hooks.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220624Z-f865060dd10d04a3","text":"W4: hcaptcha/recaptcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so --host-resolver-rules cannot point a test browser's captcha frame at a local http server (the load hangs); test captcha frame composition through extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c32ace5fe4e098f","sum":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a fixture-accepted test socket needs SO_NOSIGPIPE or a late write kills the run (signal 13). B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even with a model's tokens-per-day spent; only a real-size request shows the 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T223033Z-e64c70b59e406a7f","text":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a test socket that a fixture accept()s needs SO_NOSIGPIPE, or a write after the peer closed kills the whole run with signal 13, blamed on whichever test was running.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-04a43869ad872043","text":"B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even when a model's tokens-per-day is spent; only a real-size request shows the 429 TPD. gpt-oss-120b's day ran out during B26's first Ask run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
